<title>FRANCE: RUGBY UNION-TOULOUSE WIN FRENCH CHAMPIONSHIP FINAL.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-TOULOUSE WIN FRENCH CHAMPIONSHIP FINAL.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toulouse beat Bourgoin 12-6 (halftime 3-3) in the French rugby union championship final at Parc des Princes on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Toulouse - Penalties: Christophe Deylaud (3). Drop-goal: Deylaud.</p>
<p>Bourgoin - Penalties: Nigel Geany (2).</p>
<p>Attendance: 48,000.</p>
